                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "6\\sqrt6",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " square units.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p45-q15-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the cosine rule to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cos A=\\frac15",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin A=\\frac{2\\sqrt6}{5}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and the triangle area rule.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "By the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos A&=\\frac{6^2+5^2-7^2}{2(6)(5)}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac15.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0^\\circ<A<180^\\circ$, $\\sin A>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin A&=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac15\\right)^2}\\\\\\sin A&=\\frac{2\\sqrt6}{5}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the triangle area rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{Area}(ABC)&=\\frac12(5)(6)\\frac{2\\sqrt6}{5}\\\\\\operatorname{Area}(ABC)&=6\\sqrt6\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By considering the area of $\\triangle AOB$, $\\triangle BOC$ and $\\triangle COA$, show that $r=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt6}{3}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p45-q15-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "r=\\frac{2\\sqrt6}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p45-q15-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The perpendicular radii give a common height ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "r",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so the three areas sum to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac12r(5+7+6)=9r",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Equate this with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "6\\sqrt6",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Join $O$ to $A$, $B$ and $C$. Each radius to a point of tangency is perpendicular to the corresponding side, so the three triangles have height $r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{Area}(ABC)&=\\operatorname{Area}(AOB)+\\operatorname{Area}(BOC)+\\operatorname{Area}(COA)\\\\\\operatorname{Area}(ABC)&=\\frac12(5)r+\\frac12(7)r+\\frac12(6)r\\\\\\operatorname{Area}(ABC)&=9r.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}9r&=6\\sqrt6\\\\r&=\\frac{6\\sqrt6}{9}\\\\r&=\\frac{2\\sqrt6}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
